@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Shared locked CSV mutation and failure-safe replacement
hide footbox
autonumber
participant "App / collection functions\n<<caller>>" as Caller
participant "dataset.py\n<<module>>" as Dataset
participant "path-keyed FileLock\n<<external>>" as Lock
participant "Local filesystem\n<<external>>" as Files

activate Caller
Caller -> Dataset : append_entry / update_entry / delete_entry\n(or collection's outer transaction)
activate Dataset
Dataset -> Lock : acquire(timeout=10)
activate Lock
Lock --> Dataset : Lock held or Timeout
deactivate Lock
alt Lock acquired
  Dataset -> Dataset : load_all()
  activate Dataset
  note over Dataset : Reentrant same-path lock; ensure storage.\nValidate 10/11/14-field exact header and row shape.
  Dataset -> Files : Read UTF-8 CSV
  activate Files
  Files --> Dataset : Bytes / read failure
  deactivate Files
  Dataset --> Dataset : Normalized row dictionaries / error
  deactivate Dataset
  opt Read and mutation validation succeed
    note over Dataset : Missing update/delete IDs raise EntryNotFoundError.\nModify rows in memory; reset approval on changed\nfields unless review status is explicitly supplied.
    Dataset -> Dataset : _write_entries(entries)
    activate Dataset
    Dataset -> Files : Create sibling scratch file;\nwrite canonical header/rows; flush + fsync
    activate Files
    Files --> Dataset : Completed sibling or write failure
    deactivate Files
    opt Sibling completely written
      Dataset -> Files : os.replace(sibling, dataset.csv)
      activate Files
      Files --> Dataset : Atomic replacement / replacement failure
      deactivate Files
    end
    note over Dataset : Finally remove any leftover sibling.\nBefore replacement failure, previous CSV stays intact.
    Dataset --> Dataset : Committed or exception
    deactivate Dataset
  end
  Dataset -> Lock : release() in context-manager exit
  activate Lock
  Lock --> Dataset : Released, including on failure
  deactivate Lock
else Lock timed out
  note over Dataset : No mutation; return busy/failure to caller.
end
Dataset --> Caller : Success or propagated exception
deactivate Dataset
deactivate Caller
legend bottom
  collection functions take the same outer lock around duplicate/ID checks and write.
  Lock activation shows the acquire/release call, not the duration of file ownership.
  Append also rewrites the full dataset; there is no unsafe direct append path.
  Protection covers cooperative users of this path, not external manual writers.
endlegend
@enduml
